<title>SINGAPORE: India offers Mar/Apr Vizag low aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India offers Mar/Apr Vizag low aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) is offering by tender a 25,000-tonne cargo of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) from Vizag on the east coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender for the March 30-April 1 lifting cargo, closes March 13 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last Vizag LAN sale, for February 9-11 lifting, was made at the end of January at a $30.00 discount to Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
